# Conventional Commits

Use the [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/) format for every git commit in this project.

## Format

```
<type>[optional scope]: <description>

[optional body]

[optional footer(s)]
```

## Types

- **feat:** new feature (MINOR in SemVer)
- **fix:** bug fix (PATCH in SemVer)
- **build:** build system, dependencies
- **chore:** maintenance, no code change
- **ci:** CI config
- **docs:** documentation only
- **style:** formatting, no logic change
- **refactor:** code change, no feature/fix
- **perf:** performance improvement
- **test:** adding or updating tests

## Scope (optional)

Noun in parentheses for context, e.g. `feat(staging):`, `fix(dbt):`.

## Examples

```
feat(staging): add stg_accounts_created with deduplication
```

```
fix: prevent duplicate rows in account_created staging
```

```
docs: correct spelling in README
```

## Breaking changes

- In footer: `BREAKING CHANGE: <description>`
- Or append `!` after type/scope: `feat!: drop Node 6`

When the user asks to commit, write the message in this format and use it in the commit command.
